Z||000000||madspeed||12-13-2001||02:11 AM||||Ok, I had an electric cooling fan out of a Fiero, don't know what model, installed in another vehicle. I need to replace it due to an accident, can someone tell me something about what different fans are available. How many different types were used by the factory? I assume the V6 fan to be the best, does anyone know where I can pick up a replacement???||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-13-2001||10:19 PM||||I think that all fans themselves are the same, but the different speeds were obtained by having a double relay that, for low speed, would fire with a resistor in series to the power feed for the fan.  For high speed, it would just have un resisted +12v to the fan.  By that logic, 1 speed fans are just as fast as a 2 speed fan on high.<P>But, I only know this by looking at a wiring diagram, and assuming that all fans are the same...||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSoul||12-14-2001||06:41 AM||||  I can say from experience the two speed fan in my 84 is very different from the single speeds.  One difference is that the single speed sells for about $30 and the two speed (available only through Pontiac) sells for about $245.  Physically they are different too.  The 2 speed is open when you remove it from the mount not the little solid cased rig found on so many similar year GM products.  I think there were only these two types but I could be wrong.||||reg||6
Z||000003||GTDude||12-14-2001||06:17 PM||||84 model was only one to use 2 speed fan...all the rest are the same....and same speed.  If you need a complete fan assm. get a used one.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
